window.products.push({"id":136975,"name":"GE Refrigerator Auger Replacement WR17X11705 Ice Bucket Auger PS964350 General Electric Dispenser Metal Part Number AP3672963 WR17X11305 GSH25JSRFSS G","category":"homeandappliances","retail price":15.95,"sale price":null,"image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51W53k+-8wS._SL1492_.jpg","description":"💡 Ge Wr17x11705 Ice Bucket Auger - A high-quality exact equivalent for part numbers AP3672963, 1042091, AH964350, EA964350, PS964350, WR17X11305. Refrigerator Ice Dispenser Auger Wr17x11705 is compatible with General Electric, Hotpoint appliances. Wr17x11705 Ge Refrigerator Auger Replacement's main function is to rotate and move the ice cubes from the ice maker to the ice dispenser chute, so that they can be easily accessed by the user. Includes a metal rod in the center and a plastic rotator. 🔧 DIY eTips Included - Not sure how to replace the part? Helpful information can be found on the page below. Scroll down to get more repair tips. Acquire valuable skills during the DIY repair project. Ge Refrigerator Part Wr17x11705 will help if your appliance doesn't dispense or make ice, doesn't dispense water. The Wr17x11705 Auger's durable plastic material ensures a long-lasting and sturdy design. It is also designed to be easy to install, with no special tools or skills required. 💡 One of the key features of the General Electric Wr17x11705 Dispenser Auger is its helix shape. This shape is specifically designed to help move the ice cubes from the ice maker to the dispenser chute quickly and efficiently. The helix design also helps to prevent clogging or jamming of the ice cubes, which can sometimes happen with other types of augers. Wr17x11705 Ice Maker Auger meets or exceeds all manufacturer specifications. We provide a lifetime warranty and guarantee 100% money back. 💡 Why is my ice auger not working? If your ice auger is not working properly, there could be several reasons why. These include clogged ice, a faulty motor, a damaged auger blade, a loose drive mechanism, or a problem with the control board. To troubleshoot the issue, try breaking up any clumped ice, testing the power supply to the motor, checking the condition of the auger blade, tightening any loose parts, or seeking professional repair or replacement of the control board if necessary. 💡 What is the life of an auger? The life of an auger can vary depending on several factors, such as usage frequency, maintenance, and the quality of the materials used to manufacture the auger. In general, an auger can last for several years with proper maintenance and care. However, if the auger is not maintained or used frequently, it may have a shorter lifespan. Lower quality materials in the auger may lead to a shorter lifespan compared to higher quality materials.","images":["https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51W53k+-8wS._SL1492_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61zNIJh6ZCL._SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61TWUez1VxL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51TIpnkrEpL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51I6jTu8yCL._AC_SL1300_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31o9GyU6jnL._AC_.jpg"],"specifications":{"brand":"PartsBroz","source_asin":"B07J643YC3","category_path":"Home & Appliances"},"sku":"BM-136975","productType":"Home & Appliances","inventory":0,"age_group":"Adult","gender":"Unisex","source_url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B07J643YC3","source_catalog":"Amazon Reviews 2023 product metadata","source_file":"meta_Appliances.jsonl","source_asin":"B07J643YC3","price_pending":true,"merchant_ready":false});
